+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Voyage 1 — TodoMVC app
+
+**Intent**: Build a TodoMVC app from `assets/app-spec.md` using `assets/app-template.index.html` as base markup. Vanilla JS, no preprocessors, localStorage persistence.
+
+**Assets**: `assets/app-spec.md` is the authoritative spec. `assets/app-template.index.html` is the base template.
+
+**Specs written**: `features/todos.feature` — 25 scenarios covering all functional areas:
+- Empty state display
+- Creating todos (with trim, empty validation)
+- Completing/reactivating
+- Mark all as complete
+- Editing (enter, blur, escape, empty destroy)
+- Deleting
+- Todo count/pluralization
+- Routing (#/, #/active, #/completed)
+- Persistence
+- localStorage format
+
+**Production code needed** (not yet written):
+- `index.html` — from template, clean up comments and sample items
+- `css/app.css` — optional style overrides
+- `js/app.js` — vanilla JS app with localStorage persistence and hash routing
+
+**Watchbill**: `watchbill.json` lists all 25 scenarios in a single watch group.
+
+**Next**: QM reads the feature specs and verifies against the production code once built. Dispatch QM after `index.html`, `js/app.js`, and `css/app.css` are written.
+
+**Open questions**: None.
