+Feature: TodoMVC app
+  As a user
+  I want to manage a todo list
+  So that I can keep track of tasks I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  # ─── Display state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: No todos shows empty state
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    Then "#main" should be hidden
+    And "#footer" should be hidden
+
+  # ─── Creating todos ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then I should see 1 todo in the list
+    And the new-todo input should be cleared
+
+  Scenario: Empty input is ignored
+    When I type "   " into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list should still be empty
+
+  Scenario: Trims whitespace from input
+    When I type "  Buy eggs  " into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then I should see a todo with title "Buy eggs"
+
+  # ─── Completing todos ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: Complete a todo
+    Given I have a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo should have class "completed"
+    And the "Buy milk" todo should have its "completed" property set
+
+  Scenario: Reactivate a completed todo
+    Given I have a completed todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo should not have class "completed"
+
+  # ─── Mark all as complete ────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete toggles all todos
+    Given I have todos: "Buy milk", "Buy eggs", "Pay bills"
+    When I click the "toggle-all" checkbox
+    Then all todos should be marked completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all updates when individual todos are checked
+    Given I have todos: "Buy milk", "Buy eggs", "Pay bills"
+    When I complete all todos individually
+    Then the "toggle-all" checkbox should be checked
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button hides after clearing
+    Given I have a completed todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And I have an active todo titled "Buy eggs"
+    When I click "Clear completed"
+    Then there should be 1 todo in the list
+    And the "Clear completed" button should be hidden
+
+  # ─── Editing todos ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: Double-click enters editing mode
+    Given I have a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo item should have class "editing"
+    And the edit input for "Buy milk" should be focused
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on Enter
+    Given I am editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When I change the edit input value to "Buy oat milk"
+    And I press Enter in the edit input
+    Then I should see a todo with title "Buy oat milk"
+    And the "Buy milk" todo item should not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on blur
+    Given I am editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When I change the edit input value to "Buy oat milk"
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then I should see a todo with title "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Cancel edit with Escape
+    Given I am editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When I change the edit input value to "Buy oat milk"
+    And I press Escape in the edit input
+    Then I should see a todo with title "Buy milk"
+    And the "Buy milk" todo item should not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    Given I am editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When I change the edit input value to ""
+    And I press Enter in the edit input
+    Then the todo list should be empty
+
+  # ─── Destroying todos ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: Delete a todo with destroy button
+    Given I have a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list should be empty
+
+  # ─── Todo count ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: Todo count shows active items
+    Given I have a completed todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And I have an active todo titled "Buy eggs"
+    Then the todo-count should show "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Todo count is pluralized
+    Given I have todos: "Buy milk", "Buy eggs"
+    Then the todo-count should show "2 items left"
+
+  # ─── Routing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: All route shows all todos
+    Given I have a completed todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And I have an active todo titled "Buy eggs"
+    When I navigate to "#/"
+    Then I should see 2 todos in the list
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+    Given I have a completed todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And I have an active todo titled "Buy eggs"
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then I should see 1 todo in the list
+    And the filter link for "Active" should have class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given I have a completed todo titled "Buy milk"
+    And I have an active todo titled "Buy eggs"
+    When I navigate to "#/completed"
+    Then I should see 1 todo in the list
+    And the filter link for "Completed" should have class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Item hidden when filter changes after update
+    Given I have an active todo titled "Buy eggs"
+    And I navigate to "#/active"
+    When I complete the todo "Buy eggs"
+    Then I should see 0 todos in the list
+
+  # ─── Persistence ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist across page reloads
+    Given I have a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I reload the app
+    Then I should see a todo with title "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Completed state persists
+    Given I have a completed todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When I reload the app
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo should have class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given I am editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When I reload the app
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo item should not have class "editing"
+
+  # ─── localStorage format ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Scenario: Uses correct storage key format
+    Given I have a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage should contain a key matching "todos-"
+
+  Scenario: Todo items have required fields in localStorage
+    Given I have a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage todo data should include fields "id", "title", "completed"
